:c_13 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        tido:Consideration ;
    rdf:value "For every means you would like to deploy, it is important to put your thoughts on paper as not only Ton, but also the minister and everyone else involved in the safeguard ladder to know what is going on in your head"^^xsd:string ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy :evaluation_16 ;
    tido:supports :c_17 .

:c_14 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        tido:Consideration ;
    rdf:value "You must always ask yourself whether if that what you want to do is necessary, whether it is proportional (i.e. how does the impact of the means relate to the threat of the situation), and whether it is subsidiary (i.e. could you achieve the same with a lighter means)."^^xsd:string ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy :evaluation_16 ;
    tido:supports :c_17 .

:c_6 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        tido:Consideration ;
    rdf:value "These options are substantial"^^xsd:string ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy :evaluation_10 .

:c_7 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        tido:Consideration ;
    rdf:value "These options are indeed substantial, and it shows that the analyst is the biggest safeguard. "^^xsd:string ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy :evaluation_11 .

:c_8 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        tido:Consideration ;
    rdf:value "As the analyst is the one that chooses which means to deploy, he or she needs to be very aware of why those means need to be deployed and whether it is not possible to obtain the information ins another way "^^xsd:string ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy :evaluation_11 ;
    tido:supports :c_10 .

:c_9 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        tido:Consideration ;
    rdf:value "At this point, Sander could still be an interested chemistry student. "^^xsd:string ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy :evaluation_12 ;
    tido:supports :c_10 .

